# 20. Research Gaps

The baseline identifies several areas requiring deeper investigation.

### 20.1 National restoration spending

A comprehensive cross-agency estimate of restoration investment is needed.

### 20.2 Outcome measurement

Which programs systematically measure biological and ecosystem-level outcomes?

### 20.3 Cost-effectiveness

Which restoration interventions produce the greatest ecological improvement per dollar?

### 20.4 Maintenance

How frequently do restored systems require continued intervention?

### 20.5 Private-land durability

How long do restoration benefits persist after financial assistance ends?

### 20.6 Landscape connectivity

Which project portfolios produce measurable landscape-scale benefits?

### 20.7 Attribution

How confidently can ecological improvement be attributed to restoration rather than external environmental change?

### 20.8 Workforce

Where are technical and implementation capacity constraints most severe?

### 20.9 Tribal restoration

Which institutional arrangements produce durable ecological and governance outcomes?

### 20.10 Climate and changing ecological baselines

When historical reference conditions are no longer attainable or desirable, how should restoration objectives be established?

